.TH BONGOCAT 1 "October 2026" "bongocat 2.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bongocat \- bongo cat overlay for Wayland that plays along with the keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bongocat
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bongocat
shows an animated cat in a bar on wlr-layer-shell compositors. Its paws follow
key presses on every keyboard, including keyboards connected later. Only one
instance runs per user.
.PP
Keyboards are read by a helper process that reports only which paw to move,
never which key was pressed. Reading
.I /dev/input
requires membership in the
.B input
group, a device ACL, or a setgid installation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Configuration file. Otherwise the first readable of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bongocat/bongocat.conf ,
.I ~/.config/bongocat/bongocat.conf
and
.I ./bongocat.conf
is used; without one, defaults apply.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch\-config
Reload the configuration 300 ms after it changes, including atomic
replacement and symlink changes.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monitor " " \fINAME\fR
Show the cat only on monitor
.IR NAME ,
overriding
.BR monitor .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-toggle
Stop the running instance; if none runs, start one.
.TP
.BR \-\-hide ", " \-\-show
Hide or show every overlay of the running instance.
.TP
.BR \-\-pause ", " \-\-resume
Show the idle frame and ignore input, or resume.
.TP
.B \-\-reload
Reload the configuration of the running instance. An invalid file keeps the
running configuration and fails.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Describe the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Strictly validate the configuration. A missing file is valid when no
.B \-c
was given.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-devices
List input devices, mark keyboards, and print matching
.B keyboard_name
and
.B keyboard_device
lines.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-monitors
List monitor names, sizes and scales.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Combine the three checks above with compositor protocol support.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-v ", " \-\-version
Show help or the version.
.PP
Control options reach the running instance through a socket in
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
that only the same user may use. They exit nonzero on failure.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Lines are
.IB key = value\fR;
lines starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
and text after whitespace followed by
.B #
are comments.
.B [monitor:\fINAME\fB]
starts a section overriding the appearance settings for one monitor, and
.B [global]
returns to global settings. At startup invalid lines are skipped with a
warning; reloads and
.B \-\-check\-config
reject the whole file instead.
.SS Appearance (allowed in monitor sections)
.TP
.BR cat_height " (10\(en200, default 40)"
Cat height in pixels.
.TP
.BR cat_align " (left, center, right; default center)"
Horizontal alignment.
.TP
.BR cat_x_offset ", " cat_y_offset " (default 100, 10)"
Offset from the alignment and from the bar's vertical center.
.TP
.BR overlay_height " (20\(en300, default 50)"
Bar height in pixels.
.TP
.BR overlay_opacity " (0\(en255, default 150)"
Bar background opacity.
.TP
.BR overlay_position " (top, bottom; default top)"
Screen edge.
.TP
.BR layer " (background, bottom, top, overlay; default top)"
Layer-shell layer.
.TP
.BR mirror_x ", " mirror_y " (0, 1; default 0)"
Flip the cat horizontally or vertically.
.TP
.BR disable_fullscreen_hide " (0, 1; default 0)"
By default a cat hides while the window most recently focused on its monitor
is fullscreen, and reappears when an empty workspace gains focus there. 1 keeps
it visible, as does
.BR layer=overlay .
.SS Monitors
.TP
.B monitor
Comma-separated monitor names, each showing a cat; disconnected monitors are
waited for. Empty (default) shows one cat on an automatically chosen monitor.
.TP
.BR follow_active_monitor " (0, 1; default 1)"
In automatic mode, follow the monitor of the focused window, from
wlr-foreign-toplevel-management. Under niri
.RB ( NIRI_SOCKET )
the focused monitor comes from niri's event stream and includes empty
workspaces. Without focus information the cat stays where it is. 0 uses the
first monitor.
.SS Keyboards
.TP
.B keyboard_device
Device path inside
.IR /dev/input/ ,
such as a stable
.I by-id
link. Repeatable.
.TP
.B keyboard_name
Read devices whose name contains this text. Repeatable.
.PP
Without either, every keyboard is read.
.SS Animation and sleep
.TP
.BR fps " (1\(en120, default 60)"
Maximum frame changes per second.
.TP
.BR keypress_duration " (10\(en5000 ms, default 100)"
How long a paw stays down.
.TP
.BR enable_hand_mapping " (0, 1; default 1)"
Keys on the left half of the keyboard play the left paw; 0 picks a random
paw.
.TP
.BR idle_frame " (0\(en4, default 0)"
Frame shown while idle.
.TP
.BR test_animation_interval ", " test_animation_duration " (default 0 s, 200 ms)"
Tap a paw every interval without input; 0 disables.
.TP
.BR idle_sleep_timeout " (0\(en3600 s, default 0)"
Show the sleeping cat after this long without input; 0 disables.
.TP
.BR enable_scheduled_sleep ", " sleep_begin ", " sleep_end " (default 0, 00:00, 00:00)"
Sleep daily between two HH:MM times, ignoring key presses.
.TP
.BR enable_debug " (0, 1; default 0)"
Debug logging. Key presses are never logged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bongocat.pid
Single-instance lock.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bongocat.sock
Control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
Example configuration:
.I /usr/share/bongocat/bongocat.conf.example
or the
.I share/bongocat
directory of the installation prefix.
